          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "## Finding: the event-level review is incomplete\n\nI identified the relevant Racine work order and the exact Pending Close timestamp, but **cannot verify whether a late event exists** from the records I’m authorized to read.\n\n| Requested item | Verified result |\n|---|---|\n| Manufacturing order | **MO-25-09-1070** |\n| Work order ID | **WO-2025-09-004** |\n| Operation/product | Modine Racine–Dekoven; **Cooler Plate Pack** |\n| September cost period | **Sep-25 — PER-COST-2025-09** |\n| Exact Pending Close time | **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** — no timezone specified in the source |\n| Source transaction ID | Not available in the accessible extract |\n| Event amount | Not available |\n| Exact event-created time | Not available |\n| Minutes late | Cannot calculate without the event-created time |\n| Recorded accounting status | Not available |\n| Status consistent with policy? | **Undetermined without event evidence** |\n\nThe accessible extract contains work-order and cost-period records, but **no cost-event rows**. The supporting records are restricted to a records custodian. I requested an authorized extract but did not receive one. The absence of visible event rows is **not evidence that no late event occurred**.\n\n### Oracle’s documented treatment\n\nOracle Fusion Cloud SCM Cost Management 26B, **“Cost Accounting Period Statuses and Transaction Accounting,” PDF page 233 / printed page 225**, states that:\n\n- New transactions falling in the Pending Close period or an earlier period are not staged in Cost Accounting or Receipt Accounting; they are processed after the period is closed or reopened.\n- Transactions entered before Pending Close continue to be processed, including those in error.\n- **Revenue lines, COGS recognition, and manual cost adjustments are exceptions** and continue to be processed.\n\nAccordingly, an ordinary, non-exempt transaction created after **`2025-09-30T18:00:00`** should be held from processing while that Pending Close hold remains in effect. Its event type, creation time, and recorded accounting status are necessary to reach a defensible consistency conclusion.\n\n**No database records were changed.** I submitted the incomplete audit with status **`needs_evidence`** and saved the result and provenance at:\n\n`/cache/work/worker_144079c62761/audit-report.json`\n\nCompletion requires a custodian-approved cost-event extract for **WO-2025-09-004**, including the source transaction ID, amount, event type, creation timestamp, and accounting status.",
          "annotations": [],
          "logprobs": []
        }
      ],
